  "content": {
    "id": "p24-q12-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "Anna is running laps around a circular track and completes each circuit in 99 seconds. Billy runs in the other direction and passes Anna every 45 seconds. How long does it take Billy to run around the track?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$82.5$ seconds.\n\nTheir circuit rates add because they run in opposite directions.",
      "worked": "Let $t$ seconds be Billy's lap time. Anna runs $\\frac{45}{99}$ of a circuit in 45 seconds. Between meetings, their combined distance is one circuit.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{45}{99}+\\frac{45}{t}&=1\\\\\\frac{45}{t}&=1-\\frac{5}{11}\\\\\\frac{45}{t}&=\\frac{6}{11}\\\\6t&=495\\\\t&=\\frac{165}{2}=82.5\\end{align*}$$\n\nBilly takes $82.5$ seconds to run around the track.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 74
  },
